{
  "version": 1,
  "purpose": "The other names people say for an installed application, folded (no accents, lower case): «spoken» are the words said, «catalog» the Start catalog names they stand for, tried in order (the first one installed wins). «aliases» serve every reader (app.open and computer use, semantic.catalog._CATALOG_NAME_ALIASES); «mission_aliases» only the computer-use readers (semantic.missions._EXTRA_ALIASES), where a word like «configuracion» is the Settings window and not an order to open it. An application's own name, a unique subset of its words or one near spelling needs no row (missions._catalog_key). «companion_words» make a Start entry the companion of an application (its help, uninstaller, readme or website), never the application said when the application itself is also named. «common_words» are ordinary words (folded, singular) one letter away from an application's one-word name («stream» and Steam, «print» and Paint): a near spelling never reaches a name from them, and alone they never reach a name that only starts or ends with them («de la pantalla» is no «Teclado en pantalla»), nor are they the one word that tells a name apart (missions.resolve_application). «folder_application» are the catalog names, tried in order, of the application that shows a folder of the person's: an order said in a folder and in no application is done there (missions._in_named_folder).",
